[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_8e4b022304d67b5b\",\"r_60a44b76938a3e04\"],null,null,[[\"rc_8b052bde0ee9dc18\",[\"Expert consensus and Wall Street models project SpaceX’s valuation to settle between **$1.3 trillion and $1.8 trillion** by the end of 2026, though market pricing has experienced significant volatility around the $1.5T–$2.1T mark.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Valuation Scenarios (Year-End 2026)\\n\\n| Scenario | Implied Valuation | Core Assumptions / Drivers |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bull Case** | **$2.0T – $2.5T+** | Rapid cadence of operational Starship launches; accelerated Starlink direct-to-cell adoption; higher tech multiples. |\\n| **Base Case** | **$1.4T – $1.7T** | Sustained Starlink subscriber growth (approaching run-rate profitability); steady Falcon 9 cadence; multiple compression toward sum-of-parts fair value. |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$780B – $1.25T** | Discounted cash flow (DCF) fundamentals taking precedence post-lockup expiry; technical delays on Starship; public market multiple contraction. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n1. **Starlink Scaling \\u0026 Direct-to-Device (D2D):** Starlink represents the lion's share of cash flow expansion. Integration of acquired mobile satellite spectrum (e.g., EchoStar assets) into commercial carrier partnerships accelerates recurring consumer and enterprise telecom revenue.\\n2. **Starship Operational Milestones:** Successful orbital deployment of Starlink V3 satellites via Starship significantly expands network bandwidth per launch, drastically lowering launch cost per kilogram.\\n3. **Defense \\u0026 Government Contracts:** Ongoing expansion of national security space architecture (Starshield) and crewed/cargo contracts with NASA providing high-visibility, counter-cyclical revenue streams.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Downside Risks\\n\\n1. **Float Expansion \\u0026 Lockup Expiry:** The expiration of insider share lockups (e.g., standard 180-day post-offering windows) materially increases tradable float, creating technical selling pressure on equity pricing.\\n2. **Capital Expenditure \\u0026 Free Cash Flow Burn:** Scaling the Starship manufacturing complex and satellite constellation replacement cycle requires massive reinvestment, pressuring near-term free cash flow margins.\\n3. **Regulatory \\u0026 Orbital Congestion Constraints:** Increased scrutiny from the FAA and FCC concerning orbital debris, spectrum interference\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://satnews.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://satnews.com/2025/12/10/spacex-targeting-1-5-trillion-valuation-ahead-of-potential-2026-ipo/\",\"SpaceX Targeting $1.5 Trillion Valuation Ahead of Potential 2026 IPO\",null,[]],[\"https://t2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://sacra.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://sacra.com/c/spacex/valuation/\",\"SpaceX: $800.00B valuation [2026] - Sacra\",null,[]],[\"https://t2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://futuresearch.ai/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://futuresearch.ai/spacex-ipo-valuation/\",\"SpaceX IPO Price and Stock Forecast to 2027 - FutureSearch.ai\",null,[]],[\"https://t2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://valueaddvc.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://valueaddvc.com/blog/spacex-valuation-2026-from-350b-tender-offer-t